# CVE-2026-65885 — Joomla Gridbox < 2.20.2 Authenticated Arbitrary File Upload
#
# SEVERITY DISCREPANCY: NVD [1] reports CVSS 0 (NONE / not yet scored),
# while CVE.org CNA-published record [5] reports CVSS v4.0 score of 9.4
# (CRITICAL). Analysts should treat the CNA score [5] as the more
# authoritative signal until NVD completes its analysis. Do not rely on
# the NVD score for triage at this time.
#
# KEV STATUS: Actively exploited in the wild per VulnCheck KEV, added
# 2026-07-29 [2]. Prioritise accordingly despite missing NVD scoring.
#
# PoC status: No public PoC known — pattern inferred from the
# CVE/advisory description only.
#
# PCAP status: No packet-capture (PCAP) data source is available to
# this pipeline — this pattern is NOT verified against captured exploit
# traffic.
#
# Pattern rationale: The vulnerability is an authenticated arbitrary file
# upload in the Gridbox Joomla extension (balbooa.com) [3][4][5].
# Joomla component requests typically route through index.php with the
# "option=com_gridbox" parameter. The upload endpoint is expected to
# accept multipart POST requests. This rule targets multipart file upload
# POSTs to the Gridbox component URI. Because no PoC or PCAP is
# available, the match logic is inferred from the vulnerability class
# (insecure file upload) and Joomla component routing conventions only.
# Confidence in match accuracy is LOW. Analyst review is strongly
# advised before any deployment, especially given active exploitation [2].
#
# DRAFT — FOR ANALYST REVIEW ONLY. Do not deploy to production without
# validation against environment-specific traffic baselines.
#
alert http $EXTERNAL_NET any -> $HOME_NET any (
  msg:"THREATFORGE CVE-2026-65885 Joomla Gridbox authenticated arbitrary file upload attempt";
  flow:established,to_server;
  http.method; content:"POST";
  http.uri; content:"option=com_gridbox"; nocase;
  http.request_body; content:"Content-Disposition|3a 20|form-data"; nocase;
  pcre:"/filename\s*=\s*[\"'][^\"']+\.(php[3-7]?|phtml|phar|shtml|cgi|pl|py|sh|asp|aspx|jsp)[\"']/i";
  reference:cve,2026-65885;
  metadata:mitre_technique_id T1190, is_kev true, status experimental;
  classtype:web-application-attack; sid:9004201; rev:1; )

